				- Connect to EC2 Instance ::::
				
					To connect to Linux instance we use 
					
						- SecureSHell(SSH) Connection
						
						- port 22 
						
					- Parameters required to enable SSH connection

						- HostName 				# Public IP Address 
						
						- UserName				# Default Linux User Name 

						- User Credentials: (Authentication Types)
							- Password based Authentication
							- Token based Authentication
							- Key based Authentication
								- Private Key 					# *.pem
								- Public Key 
								- authorized_keys
							- Passwordless Authentication
							
				- Login to EC2 Instance :::
				
					- EC2 Instance Connect 				# Thru Web Browser
					
					- SSH Agent :						# Windows Users 
					
						- Putty 
						- MobaXTerm						# Windows Users 
							==> https://mobaxterm.mobatek.net/download-home-edition.html	
							
					- Terminal :						# Window/Mac/Linux

							Open the Terminal.

							Locate your private key file. The key used to launch this instance is AWS_MLOps_KeyPair.pem

							Run this command, if necessary, to ensure your key is not publicly viewable.
							chmod 400 "AWS_MLOps_KeyPair.pem"

							Example:

							ssh -i "AWS_MLOps_KeyPair.pem" ubuntu@ec2-13-126-190-242.ap-south-1.compute.amazonaws.com
